WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.220
If you're a Nintendo fan, you don't want a
Super NES Classic Edition console.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.860
You NEED a Super NES Classic Edition Console.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.420
From bona fide classics like Super Mario World
to the never-before released Star Fox 2, the

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.960
Super NES Classic is going to be the must-have
product of 2017 when it officially launches

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:17.720
in September.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.660
While most stores sold out of Super NES Classic
pre-orders pretty much immediately, it's not

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.780
quite time to panic — yet.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.470
You can still get a Super NES Classic.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.020
It's just going to take a lot of time, attention,
and patience — or a lot of money.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:32.980
Your choice.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.040
Heading to eBay

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.120
The most reliable way to get a Super NES Classic
is to buy one from scalpers on eBay.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.440
Just be warned: it's going to cost you.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.640
Consider how 2016's limited edition NES Classic,
which was manufactured in even smaller quantities

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.680
than the Super NES Classic, retailed at $60.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.740
Officially, it sold out everywhere.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.000
But savvy buyers turned to eBay to sell off
their extra consoles — and ticked up the

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.780
price tag to three or four times the original
asking price.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.530
Judging by the few Super NES Classics already
listed on eBay, it looks like that trend is

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:07.520
going to continue.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:14.060
As of the making of this video, prices fall
between $200 and $350, which is a mint higher

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.360
than the MSRP of 80 bucks.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.540
A price hike like that feels almost like an
assault.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.360
"Yeah.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.200
That's what happens, man.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.000
That's what happens."

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.140
But since everyone wants this console, sellers
are going to milk you for every buck they

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:29.660
can.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.740
If you do decide to go the eBay route, here's
some advice: Look closely at the photos and

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.280
make sure that you're getting an actual Super
NES Classic.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.860
Between customized consoles meant to imitate
the official Nintendo product and straight-up

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.640
fraudulent listings, with a little close inspection
you'll be able to tell the difference between

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.860
the new mini-console with pre-loaded games
and some imposter version.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.860
Amazon third-party sellers

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.060
You can also try to buy a Super NES Classic
from one of Amazon's third-party merchants.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:04.790
As with eBay, these are individuals or small
companies who got their hands on a Super NES

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.000
Classic and decided to resell it, usually
at a marked-up price.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.700
The Super NES Classic isn't listed yet on
Amazon's partner stores, but it should be

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.760
once the console comes out on September 29,
2017.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.840
As with eBay, make sure that you're getting
the right product.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.460
If it somehow says "games not included," it's
a no-go, because this thing should include:

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.590
"Over 20 awesome games."

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.280
Also, try to stick to merchants with high
ratings and lots of reviews.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.140
Hey, you might even get free shipping thrown
in on the deal.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.340
Run, don't walk, to GameStop

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.190
If you live in a relatively remote area, check
out your local GameStop.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:44.040
While the company sold out of Super NES Classics
online almost immediately, the brick and mortar

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.900
stores accepted pre-orders too.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.720
The catch was that you just had to go to the
store in person.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.069
By now, most GameStops in major urban areas
have probably burned through their pre-order

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:57.640
allotments, but areas that are less densely
populated might still have a few pre-order

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.440
slots open.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:03.320
Once again, however, be prepared to pay a
little more than Super NES Classic's $80 asking

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:03.840
price.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.300
GameStop knows that the mini console is a
hot item, and some customers say that they

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.480
had to buy pricier bundles with other merchandise
to get their pre-orders in.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.760
Monitor the web

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:18.160
If you want to know when more Super NES Classic
units become available, keep your Twitter

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.420
feed open at all times.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.880
When the first round of pre-orders went live,
journalists, publications, and gaming personalities

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.000
quickly let their followers know right away.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.880
If someone beat you to the punch, that's probably
why.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:34.540
Twitter feeds devoted exclusively to video
game deals also helped spread the news.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:39.220
If more pre-orders become available, or if
extra copies arrive on release day, those

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.500
same accounts will probably let you know ASAP.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.810
Of course, if you look away from Twitter for
a mere second, you risk missing the opportunity

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:50.160
to score a pre-order, so you should probably
only rely on this technique if you're already

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.600
a social media addict.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.160
"Did you see the memo about this?"

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.560
Same goes for those stock-tracking websites.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:01.680
Sites like NowInStock.net routinely update
to let readers know if and when more pre-orders

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.420
become available, so refresh, refresh, and
refresh again.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:06.780
Don't give up

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:11.540
Even if you didn't score a pre-order, you
might be able to get a Super NES Classic in

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.880
stores when it officially releases on September
29th.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.100
"Never give up.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.080
Trust your instincts."

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:23.060
Toys R Us, for example, says that it won't
have any online pre-orders for the machine,

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:27.520
while GameStop promises that it'll have a
few units available for walk-ins on launch

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.140
day, too.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:32.880
If you do decide that an in-person purchase
is your strategy of choice, just make sure

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.160
to get to the store early.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.520
Very, very early.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.440
Especially if you live in a big city, you
won't be the only person there, and most stores

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.020
tend to handle big releases like this on a
first-come, first-served basis.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.620
Import a copy

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.840
This won't work if you want to be one of the
very first people to own a Super NES Classic,

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.200
but if you're in a pinch, you can always try
to import a console from overseas.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.220
For example, while the NES Classic is sold
out in the United States, you can still pick

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:02.820
up a Nintendo Classic Mini Famicom — the
Japanese edition of the device — from the

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.920
popular international retailer Play-Asia.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.560
You will be making some sacrifices, of course.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:12.060
If your desire for a Super NES Classic hinges
on nostalgia, keep in mind that you'll be

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:16.660
getting a version modeled on the Japanese
edition of the Super NES, which looks different

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:17.880
than the American version.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.720
Think outside the box

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:25.960
Everyone is checking big outlets like GameStop,
Best Buy, and Walmart for the Super NES Classic,

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.480
but that's not the only place you'll be able
to buy one.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.180
ThinkGeek, purveyor of nerd-related novelty
items,

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.800
offered a handful of Super NES Classic bundles
that lasted a little bit longer than the other

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:36.320
options.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.800
Meanwhile, B&amp;H Photo and Video, which mainly
focuses on camera equipment, offered a few

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.120
consoles as well.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:46.320
Once the Super NES Classic comes out, don't
forget to check off-the-wall brick and mortar

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.240
stores, either.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.920
Last year, the NES Classic appeared at Urban
Outfitters, which is primarily a clothing

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.640
store for hipsters with money.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.550
If there's any kind of shop nearby that dabbles
in cool and trendy tech, or appeals to those

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:02.380
on the cutting edge of style, it might be
worth asking the cashier or manager if they're

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.400
going to have the Super NES Classic in stock.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:05.480
"What?

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:06.280
You never told me that before."

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.240
It's a long shot, but who knows?

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.820
You might strike hidden gold.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:10.920
Thanks for watching!

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.819
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:13.819 --> 00:06:16.139
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

